---
title: "Baked Tahini Meatballs, Chickpeas & Peppers"
summary: "A one-dish dinner of seasoned beef meatballs roasted over peppers, zucchini and chickpeas, finished with a lemony tahini drizzle."
publishedDate: 2026-10-01
heroImage: /images/recipes/baked-tahini-meatballs-chickpeas-peppers.webp
meal: dinner
cta: book-consult
prepMinutes: 15
cookMinutes: 25
servings: "4 servings"
ingredients:
  - "2 red bell peppers, seeds removed, sliced"
  - "1 medium zucchini, sliced into spears"
  - "1 small yellow onion, sliced"
  - "2 cups chickpeas (1 can, cooked)"
  - "1 Tbsp extra virgin olive oil"
  - "1 lb extra lean ground beef"
  - "1 tsp sea salt, to taste"
  - "1/2 tsp black pepper"
  - "2 Tbsp coconut aminos"
  - "1 1/2 tsp cumin"
  - "1 tsp paprika"
  - "1 1/2 tsp onion powder"
  - "1/4 cup tahini"
  - "1/3 cup water"
  - "1 medium lemon, juiced"
  - "2 Tbsp parsley, chopped"
steps:
  - "Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C). In a deep baking dish, add the peppers, zucchini, onion and chickpeas. Toss with olive oil and a pinch of salt and pepper. Roast the veggies for 10-15 minutes while you form the meatballs."
  - "In a bowl, combine the beef, coconut aminos, cumin, paprika, onion powder, 3/4 tsp salt and 1/4 tsp black pepper. Form meatballs, approximately 2 oz each."
  - "Remove the baking dish from the oven, place the meatballs on top of the roasted veggies and return the dish to the oven. Bake for 15 minutes. Meanwhile, in a bowl, whisk the tahini, water and lemon juice with a pinch of salt and pepper."
  - "Remove the baking dish from the oven and drizzle half of the tahini mixture over the top. Return to the oven and cook for another 5 minutes, until everything is cooked through and the flavors have combined."
  - "Remove from the oven and sprinkle with parsley. Serve the remaining tahini sauce on the side. Enjoy!"
---

A simple sheet-pan style dinner that pairs protein, fiber and healthy fats to keep blood sugar steady.

**Leftovers:** Refrigerate in an airtight container for up to three days.

**Serving size:** One serving is approximately two meatballs with 2/3 cup of peppers, chickpeas and sauce.

**More flavor:** Add garlic to the sauce and additional veggies such as broccoli or cauliflower.

**Additional toppings:** Sesame seeds.
